### Correct Function

To fix the bug, we need to modify the condition to check if the vector's length matches the number of columns in the matrix. Here's the corrected version of the function:

```java
@Override
public void set(AVector a) {
    if (cols != a.length()) {
        throw new IllegalArgumentException(
                ErrorMessages.incompatibleBroadcast(a, this));
